# Supabase — get these from your project dashboard at supabase.com
# Settings → API → Project URL and anon key
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# Optional locally, REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION for the "Delete account"
# feature (Profile → Settings → Danger zone) to work — the app itself
# uses it in app/api/account/delete/route.ts, the only place in the app
# (not tests) that needs it, to actually remove a user from Supabase.
# Also used by:
#  - tests/workbench-pro.spec.ts, to grant a disposable test account Pro
#    in the database, bypassing Stripe, to test reordering workspace
#    tabs (a Pro-only feature) — skips itself automatically without it.
#  - tests/global-teardown.ts, to delete the test accounts the Playwright
#    suite creates (*@wrench-test.dev) after the full run — silently does
#    nothing without it.
# Get it from Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API → "service_role" key
# (NOT the anon key — this one bypasses row-level security, keep it out
# of version control and only ever put it in your own .env.local, never
# here). On Vercel, add it separately under Project Settings →
# Environment Variables — this file and GitHub Actions secrets are not
# read by Vercel.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here
